phase P3
title Core
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:** the core's first slices on production: the consolidation, lane policies, Runtime life, write-ahead,
    restore, the compiler and actor identity. The core and its checks grow together, one area at a time.

    **Starts when:** P2's completion audit passes, so one test style is left and generated Stories exist. The
    orchestrator then opens this phase's Tasks.

    **Order:** @task.V3.T54, @task.V3.T18, @task.V3.T55, @task.V3.T19, @task.V3.T20, @task.V3.T17, @task.V3.T9, the
    order the user set. A `blocked_by` link is a real dependency only; where several Tasks are ready, take the
    earliest in this order.

    **Verified by:**

    - per area, the Story tests, run rules and compile-time tests written from its Spec, in
      `packages/flow-state-v3/tests/`, run by `vp test`;
    - `nub run faults`: each new rule adds a planted fault to code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts, and the
      tests must catch it;
    - the suite's coverage record, started by @task.V3.T67 and extended by each Task here;
    - skill:check-task per Task; `nub run check` and `nub run lint:rules` at zero.

    **One iteration:** the next ready Task: its Spec change, written just in time; its requirements as failing
    checks, with a planted fault for each new rule; the core change; the bench; an independent skill:check-task.
    The user's page is written at each slice's close.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - every Task is done;
    - every Requirement these Tasks build has a check that passes and that failed on its planted fault;
    - `nub run faults` catches the dead core and every named fault at the final revision;
    - the suite's coverage record is updated, and an audit by a lead that did not build the suite has passed
      (skill:policy-testing#audit-a-suite);
    - the completion audit names each Plan outcome these Tasks satisfy and finds it delivered.

    **False pass:** a test written from the code instead of the Spec; a rule with no planted fault.

    **Caught by:** the review of each Task's first commit, which maps every requirement to a Spec rule, and
    `nub run faults`.

    **Gates:**

    - `nub run faults`, which rejects the dead core and the named faults in
      code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts;
    - `nub run lint:rules`, which rejects the planted violations in code:tools/flow-state-lint/imports.test.ts and
      code:tools/flow-state-lint/rules.test.ts;
    - `nub run check`.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:**

    - a guarantee change, or one that can't be met;
    - public entry-point names or a large public API change.

    **User's read:** each Spec revision; each changed expected result with its reason; small public API calls; the
    user's page at each slice's close.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-verification (prove a suite; the coverage record);
    - skill:policy-testing (the requirements as failing checks first);
    - skill:to-spec for an area's Spec change and skill:to-design per module;
    - skill:execute-task and skill:check-task per Task; skill:review at a Task's first commit and its close;
    - skill:policy-convergence at the threshold; skill:diagnose when a test fails unexplained.

    Every Task below is a draft. Before starting its lead, the orchestrator writes its full text with skill:to-task
    (requirements, approach, acceptance by Spec rule). The earlier text of each, in `wiki/tasks/V3/` at commit
    `6b9fe478`, was written for the conformance suite: it is background only, and its acceptance does not carry
    over. The old suite's known gaps for each Task are in Appendix A of
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md.
tasks
    T54
        title       Core consolidation: owed-endings ledger, one start, diff-written records, acts into evidenceOf
        status      draft
        priority    high

        description
            Finish the core consolidation: one ledger of owed endings, one `start`, records written from what each
            step touched, and every report built by `evidenceOf` from acts.

            **Why now:** most of it is in the core at this revision; the rest was paused when the conformance suite
            was deleted, and every later core Task builds on the consolidated shape.

            **Read first:** @spec.WriteLanes (its `algorithm` section: the ledger), @spec.Actors,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/ledger.ts, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/evidence-of.ts. The
            paused step's plan is `wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/t54-a3-prep-2026-11-15.md` at commit
            `4f4ac9f5`.

            **Risk:** what is left is not listed here. The first step is to read the paused plan against the code
            and write the remaining requirements as failing checks. The old Task's "production self-proof" is
            replaced by the planted faults.

            May change: `src/core/`, `src/host/`, `tests/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a consolidation that moves code without changing who owns each fact → caught by a run rule
            per fact (one delivery per ending, one writer per record) and its planted fault.
        acceptance
            - The ledger, `start`, record writes and `evidenceOf` are each the one place their work is done, shown by
              Story tests and run rules that cite @spec.WriteLanes and @spec.Actors.
            - The two known bugs of this area (a flush that holds only its own actor's record; an adopted lane's
              later endings routed against Actors R20) are fixed, and their inverted tests are flipped.
            - `nub run faults` catches every named fault; `vp test` and `nub run check` pass.
    T18
        title       Lane policies: latest, serialize and cancel, and endings split by origin (slice 1)
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T54]
        satisfies   [@plan.Operations.O3, @plan.Runtime.O2]
        description
            Build the write-lane policies `latest`, `serialize` (up to 64, then Overloaded) and `cancel` on
            production, with the `waiting` row, as rows of the lane table, and endings split by origin.

            **Why now:** production refuses every policy but `reject`.

            **Read first:** @spec.WriteLanes, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/cells.ts#table, and the reference
            `packages/flow-state-v3/prototypes/round-14/lane.ts`.

            May change: `src/core/`, `fixtures/`, `tests/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a policy whose cells are right one at a time but wrong in sequence → caught by generated
            Stories over a fixture that uses each policy.
        acceptance
            - Each policy's cells are rows of the lane table, with a Story test for each decided cell and a fixture
              that uses the policy.
            - An operation's row reads `waiting` while commits wait behind its head.
            - Each new rule has a planted fault that `nub run faults` catches.
    T55
        title       Runtime life: Life and admit replace Disposal; the final write and its 5 s bound move into the core
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T54]
        description
            Replace the core's `Disposal` and the host's lifecycle flags with one `Life` and one `admit` table, and
            move the final write and its 5 s bound from the host into the core.

            **Why now:** the Runtime's lifecycle is split between `Disposal` in the core and flags in
            `src/host/runtime.ts`, which disagree on early and late calls.

            **Read first:** @spec.Actors (R4, R22, R23), code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/disposal.ts,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/runtime.ts.

            May change: `src/core/`, `src/host/`, `tests/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: an `admit` table that is total by type but never reached for some inputs → caught by a
            Story test for each row.
        acceptance
            - One `Life` value and one total `admit` table decide whether an input runs, is dropped or is rejected;
              the host keeps no flag of its own.
            - The known bug of this area (the disposal reports Done before its final write is answered) is fixed, and
              its inverted test is flipped.
            - Each new rule has a planted fault that `nub run faults` catches.
    T19
        title       Durability: persistence edge, write-ahead and the driver (slice 2)
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T55]
        satisfies   [@plan.Persistence.O1, @plan.Persistence.O2, @plan.Persistence.O3, @plan.Persistence.O6]
        description
            Build the persistence edge, write-ahead and the Effect driver in `src/host/` from @spec.WriteAhead.

            **Why now:** the core returns work as data, and durability can be judged only once that work is run and
            its records written as the Spec says.

            **Read first:** @spec.WriteAhead, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/persist.ts,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/driver.ts.

            May change: `src/core/`, `src/host/`, `fixtures/`, `tests/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a batch rule checked only against what the runtime reports → caught by run rules that read
            what the fake store received.
        acceptance
            - The Requirements of @spec.WriteAhead this slice builds hold, shown by run rules over the fake store's
              batches and by Story tests.
            - The known bugs of this area are fixed: a re-send's retry count missing from the capture before it,
              whose inverted test is flipped; and any write discharging every dirty end, which has no reproduction
              yet and gets its test here.
            - Each new rule has a planted fault that `nub run faults` catches.
    T20
        title       Durability: restore, owed endings at boot, quarantine and forget (slice 2a)
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T19]
        satisfies   [@plan.Inspection.O2, @plan.Persistence.O4, @plan.Persistence.O5]
        description
            Build restore from @spec.Restore and @spec.Codec: reload, owed endings delivered at boot, record format
            tags, quarantine of unreadable records, and `forget`.

            **Why now:** write-ahead records exist, but a reload cannot yet restore every actor or deliver all that
            was owed.

            **Read first:** @spec.Restore, @spec.Codec, @spec.WriteAhead.

            **Risk:** Codec I7 says no lane record has a `mayHaveApplied` field, and
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts writes one. One of the two is wrong.

            May change: `src/core/`, `src/host/`, `tests/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a restore tested only at the points someone thought of → caught by the reload sweep over
            every Story.
        acceptance
            - The Requirements of @spec.Restore and @spec.Codec this slice builds hold, shown by Story tests with a
              reload and by the reload sweep.
            - Each new rule has a planted fault that `nub run faults` catches.
    T17
        title       Machine structure: Compiled, compound states, history and fields (slice 3a)
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T54]
        satisfies   [
                    @plan.Diagnostics.O1,
                    @plan.Diagnostics.O2,
                    @plan.Diagnostics.O3,
                    @plan.Diagnostics.O4,
                    @plan.Machines.O1,
                    @plan.Machines.O2,
                    @plan.Machines.O3,
                    @plan.Machines.O4,
                    @plan.Machines.O6,
                    @plan.Machines.O7,
                    @plan.Machines.O8,
                    @plan.Operations.O1,
                    @plan.Runtime.O1
                    ]
        description
            Build Compiled and the compiler from @spec.Compile and @spec.Diagnostics, with compound states, history,
            `Flow.input`, private and computed fields and the snapshot shape.

            **Why now:** production compiles only what the fixtures need; the full construction rules and the
            diagnostics are unbuilt, and every module after this reads Compiled.

            **Read first:** @spec.Compile, @spec.Diagnostics, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts.

            **Risk:** Compile I17 says a missing service is a type error, and `runtimeSetup` takes `Layer<any>`.

            May change: `src/`, `fixtures/`, `tests/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a construction rule shown only by a passing machine → caught by a compile-time test or a
            construction test for each refused form.
        acceptance
            - The Requirements of @spec.Compile and @spec.Diagnostics this slice builds hold: each "is a type error"
              has a compile-time test, and each construction refusal a test of its error.
            - The known bug of this area (a delay past 2^31 - 1 ms is armed, not refused) is fixed, and its inverted
              test is flipped.
            - Each new runtime rule has a planted fault that `nub run faults` catches.
    T9
        title       Actor identity: refs by value, lifetime, mailboxes and context (slice 4)
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T17]
        satisfies   [@plan.Runtime.O3, @plan.Runtime.O4, @plan.Runtime.O5, @plan.Runtime.O6, @plan.Runtime.O7]
        description
            Build actor identity and lifetime on production from @spec.Actors: `actorRef` by value, `createActor`,
            snapshots and their fallbacks, the send table, context waves with `onContext`, issues by source, and the
            admission bound.

            **Why now:** production has one actor shape; identity by value, the mailbox rules and context are
            unbuilt, and the browser slice (@task.V3.T58) needs them.

            **Read first:** @spec.Actors, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/incarnations.ts,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/runtime.ts.

            May change: `src/`, `fixtures/`, `tests/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: mailbox order tested with one actor → caught by Stories with several actors and generated
            interleavings.
        acceptance
            - The Requirements of @spec.Actors this slice builds hold, shown by Story tests and run rules.
            - Each new rule has a planted fault that `nub run faults` catches.
